.TH BIGSETTER 1.SH NAMEbigsetter \- Modula-2 set operations demonstration.SH SYNOPSIS\fBbigsetter\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONA demonstration of Alex Wyss's BigSet library, which gives Modula-2 setslarger than the language's own.  It builds two sets, A and B, of thenumbers 0 to 35, and shows the results of the library's operations onthem -- include and exclude, union, intersection, difference, symmetricdifference, complement and the subset tests -- printing each set as itsmembers, or\fB{}\fRwhen it is empty, and waiting for a key after each.  Ported to OS-9 withMiele Modula-2 by W. Stehling, 1988, and distributed on EFFO forum disk 8with its source.